list.item:
Fowler, Deming, Volcker;
    McNamara; Ball, Mann; Martin;
    Ackley, Okun; Bell; Staats;
    Brimmer; Califano, Bator

div.p:
Fowler opened with a brief report on the progress of the balance of payments program, results during the first half of the year, and prospects for the rest of this year and 1966. Essentially, he summarized the September 10 Cabinet Committee Report to the President (at Tab A), especially pages 1–2. His central conclusions were that:
—the Federal Reserve’s program for banks and financial institutions is working exceedingly well;
—the results of the corporate program was much less clear, with a sharp rise in direct investment during the first half and a danger of still further increases by next year.
